 "title": "Foreclosure Sales | Winona County, MN",
 "text": "Foreclosure Sales | Winona County, MN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nGovernment\nDepartments\nHow Do I...\nNotice of Data Security Incident\nSearch\nCrime Tip Information\nEmergency Management\nForeclosure Sales\nGun Permits\nJail\nInmate Roster\nInmate Visiting / Mailing Procedures\nJail Programs\nPublic Fingerprints\nCourt Ordered Bookings & Suspense Files\nWork Release\nNational Institute of Corrections Assessment\nJail Assessment & Planning\nNew Jail Documents\nBid Information\nK-9 Unit\nMedia Booking Photo Requests\nPast Sheriffs\nPolicies\nPrison Rape Elimination Act (PREA) Violation Form\nPrograms\nSmart911\nTechnology Crimes\nVolunteer Groups\nHome\nDepartments\nSheriff\nForeclosure Sales\nForeclosure Sales\nSale Procedures\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales are conducted by the Sheriff, or his designee, in an open bidding process. Sales are conducted at 10 am in the Winona County Sheriff's Office (unless otherwise specified) at:\n201 W 3rd Street\nWinona, MN 55987\nThe mortgage company's or plaintiff's attorney will bid first. Following this bid, other bidders are given an opportunity to bid. A successful bidder must have cash or certified funds (payable to the Winona County Sheriff) available to pay the Sheriff's Office at the time of the sale.\nThe successful bidder will receive a Sheriff's Certificate of Sale that lists the name of the purchaser and the amount of the purchase.\nMortgage foreclosure sales are subject to a redemption period, which is usually six months but can be as short as five weeks or as long as one year. The length of the redemption period is noted in the sale notice.\nPlease be aware that sales can and have been postponed/canceled with very little notice without adequate time to update the sale listings. If you wish to verify, please call our office at 507-457-6368.\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales - 2026 (PDF)\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales - 2025 (PDF)\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales - 2024 (PDF)\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales - 2023 (PDF)\nMortgage Foreclosure Sales - 2021 (PDF)\nView All Links\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nAgendas & Minutes\nCareer Opportunities\nFinancial Transparency\nPay Taxes Online\nRecycling\nReport a Concern\n202 West Third Street Winona, MN 55987\nPhone: 507-457-6350\nEmail: contactus@winonacounty.gov\nSheriff's Non-Emergency Line: 507-457-6491\nHelpful Links\nCounty Valuations\nAccess to Electronic License Data\nATV Registration\nDisability Parking Certificates\nDriver Compliance - Vision Report\nOrdinances\nWinona County Events Calendar\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nQuick Links\nChild Abuse and Protection\nCurbside Recycling Finder\nHighway Maps\nLandShark Map\nOpioid Response\nParcel Viewer\nProperty Taxes\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\nSMS Terms of Service\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nBESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy BESbswy\nClose ×",
